# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# MemoryBackend locks directories top-down along the *current* tree, and
# rename() (serialized by m_renameMutex) locks ancestors before descendants.
# Moving a directory changes which node is the ancestor, so TSAN's global
# lock-order graph sees A->B before the move and B->A after it, even in a
# single thread. At any instant the order is consistent, so this is not a
# real deadlock. Use with: TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/tsan.supp
deadlock:vfs::MemoryBackend::DirLock::lock
